@0    = ~The fire elemental is blocking the way to the alestore. It hovers in the least-moist corner of the cellar and shows no intention of attacking you. Its flames seem dimmer than you would expect.~
@1    = ~(You could try to trap the fire elemental in the wooden barrel, but it would likely eat through the wood rather quickly. The barrel needs a fireproof coating on the inside.)~
@2    = ~You trap the fire elemental inside the fireproof barrel.~
@3    = ~You refrain from using the barrel.~
@4    = ~Stand back, citizen. The presence of civilians on the rooftop is allowed, but we are here to ensure you stay safe.~
@5    = ~Please stay away from the beacon. The fire is dangerous in various ways.~
@6    = ~I have a trapped fire elemental here, and I will release it into the flames.~
@7    = ~We have a fire elemental situation in the kitchen's storeroom...~
@8    = ~I know that fire causes burns. What other dangers would there be?~
@9    = ~The fire attracts fire elementals? What exactly do you mean?~
@10   = ~I read about this. The fire also attracts fire elementals from outside the beacon, right?~
@11   = ~What do you do if a fire elemental comes out of the beacon flames?~
@12   = ~No worries, I will not cause any trouble.~
@13   = ~I will go wherever I want.~
@14   = ~Well, as long as you stay away from the beacon, that's fine by me.~
@15   = ~Glad to hear it.~
@16   = ~If the oil spills, it can easily cause severe burns and a large fire. Also, large fires attract fire elementals, and they are usually unpredictable. They tend to stay inside the flames, though. If they don't, I am here to make sure they do not get far.~
@17   = ~In the storeroom? I can assure you it did not emerge from the beacon flames. You need to inform the captain about this—I can't leave my post. Down there, you probably need to kill it. Here, we could push it back into the beacon flames, but I wouldn't know how to get it up here without someone getting injured.~
@18   = ~We usually push them back into the flames. It usually doesn't take much effort; the air is way too moist around here for them to travel far.~
@19   = ~Well, it's like a portal for them, or so I've heard. They can manifest in large fires like the beacon, and they can also use it to return to their home plane.~
@20   = ~I see. Be careful around the hot flames!~
@21   = ~The beacon is such a great fire! I want to be a beacon guard when I grow up!~
@22   = ~*sigh* Every time we just stand here and stare at the flames. I guess I can understand why he likes it so much, I was young once, too.~
